<template>
  <section>
    <h2 class="pdx-txt-heading section-heading">Live Demo</h2>
    <p class="pdx-txt-small pdx-ink-muted">Scroll the box below. The toolbar sticks to the top of the scroll container, and <code>pdx-change</code> says so.</p>
    <p class="pdx-txt-small affix-state" aria-live="polite">Affixed: <strong>{{ affixed ? 'yes' : 'no' }}</strong></p>
    <div class="scroll-container" id="affix-container">
      <div class="scroll-spacer">
        <p class="pdx-txt-small pdx-ink-muted">Scroll down to see the toolbar become sticky.</p>
      </div>
      <pdx-affix :offsetTop="0" target="#affix-container" @pdx-change="e => affixed = e.detail.affixed">
        <div class="sticky-bar">
          <pdx-icon name="filter" size="16"></pdx-icon>
          <strong>Sticky Toolbar</strong>
          <span class="pdx-ink-muted">— scrolls with content, then sticks</span>
        </div>
      </pdx-affix>
      <div class="scroll-content">
        <p>This content scrolls normally beneath the sticky toolbar.</p>
        <p>The <code>pdx-affix</code> component wraps any element and makes it stick to the top (or bottom) of the scroll container when the user scrolls past it.</p>
        <p>Here, inside a scroll container, it is CSS sticky: it keeps its own place in the flow, so nothing jumps.</p>
        <p>You can configure the offset from top/bottom and target a specific scroll container.</p>
        <p class="pdx-ink-muted">Keep scrolling...</p>
        <p>The state is reported by an IntersectionObserver rooted at the container — no scroll listener in this mode.</p>
        <p>When the user scrolls back up, the element returns to its normal flow position.</p>
        <p class="pdx-ink-muted">Almost there...</p>
        <p>End of scrollable content.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <details class="source-block">
      <summary>Source</summary>
      <pre class="pdx-txt-mono"><code>&lt;div class="scroll-container" id="affix-container"&gt;
  …
  &lt;pdx-affix :offsetTop="0" target="#affix-container"
    @pdx-change="e =&gt; affixed = e.detail.affixed"&gt;
    &lt;div class="sticky-bar"&gt;Sticky Toolbar&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/pdx-affix&gt;
  …
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
    </details>
  </section>
</template>

<script setup>
let affixed = $signal(false);
</script>

